WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.600
Yeah, the backend will also
retry three times.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:08.036
Wait a minute, not three
retries—it executes at

00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:11.390
most three times, including the
first attempt.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.029
Three times for the caller, three
times for the gateway,

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.540
and another three times on the
backend—one button click at

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.884
most twenty-seven times. Every
layer thinks it's

00:00:21.885 --> 00:00:24.880
being quite responsible, but
the problem is

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.273
the request timed out. The
report generation task

00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:31.390
didn't stop, and the new
request didn't carry

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:37.630
the same request ID, so the system
thinks, 'Oh, here's another one.' This isn't

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.116
resilience, this is redundant work.
First, turn off the

00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:44.350
auto-retry that was just added,
and stop submitting

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.790
more; let the queue slowly clear out.
Deduplication needs to

00:00:47.791 --> 00:00:51.230
be patched separately. Let me check
who this legacy code was

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.530
written by? Hmm, looks like this person
is right here in the group chat.

